    "body": "## Summary\n- isolate refund stale-dispatch recovery failures so a poisoned recovery record cannot starve healthy dispatchable refunds in the same scheduler tick\n- isolate payout stale-processing recovery failures so a recovery exception cannot starve healthy new payout claims\n- preserve durable financial states on recovery exceptions; the scheduler does not invent provider outcomes, restore funds or mutate ambiguous requests\n- add regression coverage for both scheduler recovery boundaries\n- lock the refund ambiguity invariant: if Stripe may already have succeeded but persisting the provider result fails locally, the error must not be reclassified as a provider failure\n\n## Financial safety\nThis change only isolates scheduler availability boundaries. It does not alter retry limits, stable provider idempotency keys, Stripe safety windows, wallet reserve/restore behavior, settlement ordering or review-required transitions.\n\n## Schema\nNo migration.\n\n## Merge gate\nMerge only after exact-head Maven/API tests, payment/payout financial smokes, CodeQL, container security and full runtime CI are green; master must remain unchanged and the branch must be 0 commits behind.",
